# Git commit author and message

When creating a git commit:

- Pass `--author="Sathyaraj Kolandasamy <sathya.ksamy.nsu@gmail.com>"` on every `git commit`.
- Do **not** change `git config`.
- Do **not** put "Cursor", "Cursor Agent", or "Generated by Cursor" in the commit message.
- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor`.

```powershell
git commit --author="Sathyaraj Kolandasamy <sathya.ksamy.nsu@gmail.com>" -m @"
Short why-focused message.
"@
```
